        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: flowering plant genera, Greek mythology, genus relationships\n- Products: Anemopaegma, Pithecoctenium\n- People: Semele, Cadmus, Harmonia, Dionysus, Zeus\n- Organizations: Bignoniaceae\n\nFacts:\n- Anemopaegma is a genus of flowering plants in the family Bignoniaceae.\n- In Greek mythology, Semele was the daughter of the Boeotian hero Cadmus and Harmonia.\n- In Greek mythology, Semele was the mortal mother of Dionysus by Zeus in one origin myth.\n- Pithecoctenium is a genus that is closely related to Bignonia and Anemopaegma.",
